{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-114260" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Determine the largest interval on which the function $f(x)={x}^{3}-3{x}^{2}$ is concave up." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14032645/state.json" "file_sha256" "032a6a43059b540d42ba578cc0fd51d00451ad0c72b6a1268551184346ad5c3b"} {"question" "q-114260" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "A function $f(x)$ is concave up on an interval $(a,b)$ if ${f}^{″}(x)>0$ for all $x\\in (a,b).$\n\nFirst, let's calculate the second derivative of $f(x)={x}^{3}-3{x}^{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =3{x}^{2}-6x \\\\ {f}^{″}(x) & =6x-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find where the function is concave up, we solve the inequality ${f}^{″}(x)>0,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n6x-6>0\\,⟹\\,x>1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)$ is concave up on $(1,\\infty ).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14032645/state.json" "file_sha256" "032a6a43059b540d42ba578cc0fd51d00451ad0c72b6a1268551184346ad5c3b"} {"question" "q-114260" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14032645/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "425d5a71c4ad064b44f858c7994519e7f6c779771f166c169d79f678eba9b755"} {"question" "q-114260" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14032645/state.json" "file_sha256" "032a6a43059b540d42ba578cc0fd51d00451ad0c72b6a1268551184346ad5c3b"} {"question" "q-114260" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(-\\infty ,1)"] ["math" "(-\\infty ,\\infty )"] ["math" "(0,1)"] ["math" "(1,\\infty )"] ["text" "The function is concave up nowhere."]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14032645/state.json" "file_sha256" "032a6a43059b540d42ba578cc0fd51d00451ad0c72b6a1268551184346ad5c3b"} {"question" "q-114260" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "(1,\\infty )"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14032645/state.json" "file_sha256" "032a6a43059b540d42ba578cc0fd51d00451ad0c72b6a1268551184346ad5c3b"} {"question" "q-344334" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Determine the **largest** interval on which the function $f(x)=6x+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+1)-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+4)$ is concave down.\n\nThe largest interval where $f(x)$ is concave down is\n$(${{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}$).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14032645/state.json" "file_sha256" "032a6a43059b540d42ba578cc0fd51d00451ad0c72b6a1268551184346ad5c3b"} {"question" "q-344334" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we notice that the domain of the function is $x\\in (-1,\\infty ).$\n\nA function $f(x)$ is concave down on an interval $(a,b)$ if ${f}^{″}(x)<0$ for all $x\\in (a,b).$\n\nFirst, let's calculate the second derivative of $f(x)=6x+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+1)-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+4)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =6+\\frac{1}{x+1}-\\frac{1}{x+4} \\\\ {f}^{″}(x) & =-\\frac{1}{(x+1)^{2}}+\\frac{1}{(x+4)^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find where the function is concave down, we solve the inequality ${f}^{″}(x)<0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{(x+1)^{2}}+\\frac{1}{(x+4)^{2}} & <0 \\\\ \\frac{1}{(x+4)^{2}} & <\\frac{1}{(x+1)^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that for $x>-1$ we have $(x+1)^{2}<(x+4)^{2},$ and thus $\\frac{1}{(x+1)^{2}}>\\frac{1}{(x+4)^{2}}.$ \n\nTherefore, $\\frac{1}{(x+4)^{2}}<\\frac{1}{(x+1)^{2}}$ is always true in the given domain, and we conclude that the largest interval where $f(x)$ is concave down is $(\\,-1,\\infty \\,).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14032645/state.json" "file_sha256" "032a6a43059b540d42ba578cc0fd51d00451ad0c72b6a1268551184346ad5c3b"} {"question" "q-344334" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14032645/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "425d5a71c4ad064b44f858c7994519e7f6c779771f166c169d79f678eba9b755"} {"question" "q-344334" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14032645/state.json" "file_sha256" "032a6a43059b540d42ba578cc0fd51d00451ad0c72b6a1268551184346ad5c3b"} {"question" "q-344334" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-1"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14032645/state.json" "file_sha256" "032a6a43059b540d42ba578cc0fd51d00451ad0c72b6a1268551184346ad5c3b"} {"question" "q-344334" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14032645/state.json" "file_sha256" "032a6a43059b540d42ba578cc0fd51d00451ad0c72b6a1268551184346ad5c3b"} {"question" "q-344334" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\infty"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14032645/state.json" "file_sha256" "032a6a43059b540d42ba578cc0fd51d00451ad0c72b6a1268551184346ad5c3b"} {"question" "q-114264" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Determine the largest interval on which the function $f(x)={e}^{1-x}+2x$ is concave down." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14032645/state.json" "file_sha256" "032a6a43059b540d42ba578cc0fd51d00451ad0c72b6a1268551184346ad5c3b"} {"question" "q-114264" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "A function $f(x)$ is concave down on an interval $(a,b)$ if ${f}^{″}(x)<0$ for all $x\\in (a,b).$\n\nFirst, let's calculate the second derivative of $f(x)={e}^{1-x}+2x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =-{e}^{1-x}+2 \\\\ {f}^{″}(x) & =-(-{e}^{1-x})={e}^{1-x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find where the function is concave down, we solve the inequality ${f}^{″}(x)<0.$ Notice that ${f}^{″}(x)={e}^{1-x}>0$ for all values of $x.$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)$ is concave down nowhere." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14032645/state.json" "file_sha256" "032a6a43059b540d42ba578cc0fd51d00451ad0c72b6a1268551184346ad5c3b"} {"question" "q-114264" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14032645/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "425d5a71c4ad064b44f858c7994519e7f6c779771f166c169d79f678eba9b755"} {"question" "q-114264" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14032645/state.json" "file_sha256" "032a6a43059b540d42ba578cc0fd51d00451ad0c72b6a1268551184346ad5c3b"} {"question" "q-114264" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(-\\infty ,-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2)"] ["math" "(-\\infty ,0)"] ["math" "(-\\infty ,\\infty )"] ["math" "(0,\\infty )"] ["text" "The function is concave down nowhere."]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14032645/state.json" "file_sha256" "032a6a43059b540d42ba578cc0fd51d00451ad0c72b6a1268551184346ad5c3b"} {"question" "q-114264" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "The function is concave down nowhere."] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14032645/state.json" "file_sha256" "032a6a43059b540d42ba578cc0fd51d00451ad0c72b6a1268551184346ad5c3b"} {"question" "q-344340" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Determine the **largest** interval on which the function $f(x)=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2x+4}$ is concave up.\n\nThe largest interval where $f(x)$ is concave up is\n$(${{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}$).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14032645/state.json" "file_sha256" "032a6a43059b540d42ba578cc0fd51d00451ad0c72b6a1268551184346ad5c3b"} {"question" "q-344340" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we notice that the domain of the function is $x\\ne -2.$\n\nA function $f(x)$ is concave up on an interval $(a,b)$ if ${f}^{″}(x)>0$ for all $x\\in (a,b).$\n\nFirst, let's calculate the second derivative of $f(x)=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2x+4}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{(2x)(2x+4)-2{x}^{2}}{(2x+4)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2x(x+4)}{(2x+4)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2{x}^{2}+8x}{(2x+4)^{2}} \\\\ {f}^{″}(x) & =\\frac{(4x+8)(2x+4)^{2}-4(2{x}^{2}+8x)(2x+4)}{(2x+4)^{4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{8(x+2)^{2}-8{x}^{2}-32x}{(2x+4)^{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{8{x}^{2}+32x+32-8{x}^{2}-32x}{(2x+4)^{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{(x+2)^{3}} \\\\  & =4(x+2)^{-3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find where the function is concave up, we solve the inequality ${f}^{″}(x)>0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4(x+2)^{-3} & >0 \\\\ (x+2)^{-3} & >0 \\\\ x+2 & >0 \\\\ x & >-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)$ is concave up on $(\\,-2,\\infty \\,).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14032645/state.json" "file_sha256" "032a6a43059b540d42ba578cc0fd51d00451ad0c72b6a1268551184346ad5c3b"} {"question" "q-344340" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14032645/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "425d5a71c4ad064b44f858c7994519e7f6c779771f166c169d79f678eba9b755"} {"question" "q-344340" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14032645/state.json" "file_sha256" "032a6a43059b540d42ba578cc0fd51d00451ad0c72b6a1268551184346ad5c3b"} {"question" "q-344340" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-2"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14032645/state.json" "file_sha256" "032a6a43059b540d42ba578cc0fd51d00451ad0c72b6a1268551184346ad5c3b"} {"question" "q-344340" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14032645/state.json" "file_sha256" "032a6a43059b540d42ba578cc0fd51d00451ad0c72b6a1268551184346ad5c3b"} {"question" "q-344340" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\infty"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14032645/state.json" "file_sha256" "032a6a43059b540d42ba578cc0fd51d00451ad0c72b6a1268551184346ad5c3b"} {"question" "q-344330" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Determine the **largest** interval on which the function $f(x)=-3{e}^{2x}+5$ is concave down.\n\nThe largest interval where $f(x)$ is concave down is\n$(${{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}$).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14032645/state.json" "file_sha256" "032a6a43059b540d42ba578cc0fd51d00451ad0c72b6a1268551184346ad5c3b"} {"question" "q-344330" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "A function $f(x)$ is concave down on an interval $(a,b)$ if ${f}^{″}(x)<0$ for all $x\\in (a,b).$\n\nFirst, let's calculate the second derivative of $f(x)=-3{e}^{2x}+5:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =-6{e}^{2x} \\\\ {f}^{″}(x) & =-12{e}^{2x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find where the function is concave down, we solve the inequality ${f}^{″}(x)<0,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-12{e}^{2x} & <0 \\\\ {e}^{2x} & >0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)$ is concave down on $(\\,-\\infty ,\\infty \\,).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14032645/state.json" "file_sha256" "032a6a43059b540d42ba578cc0fd51d00451ad0c72b6a1268551184346ad5c3b"} {"question" "q-344330" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14032645/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "425d5a71c4ad064b44f858c7994519e7f6c779771f166c169d79f678eba9b755"} {"question" "q-344330" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14032645/state.json" "file_sha256" "032a6a43059b540d42ba578cc0fd51d00451ad0c72b6a1268551184346ad5c3b"} {"question" "q-344330" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\infty"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "f